Present Manim slides natively

Purpose: lecture with Manim slides inside Rnote: import the slides of a
ManimGX scene file, write on them, and step through their animations on
the projector. Unmodified ManimGX (PyPI manimgx 0.1.1) records each
slide as a "take"; Rnote stores the take and plays it as vectors. No
browser engine, no Manim fork, no video.

Behaviour:
- Main menu Manim Slides: "Import Scene…", "Import Scene with Notes
  Column…", "Update", "Re-render All". Import runs the scene file
  through `uv run --with manimgx==0.1.1 python` (bundled driver
  record_takes.py) and places one slide per page from the page in view,
  on the document layer, so ink goes on top. The slides are the file's
  SLIDES list, else its scene classes. A toast shows the run's progress
  and stays until the slides are placed; without uv it says where to
  get it.
- Notes column: a still copy of each slide's end state on the page to
  its right, for the lecturer's notes; it stores only the still frame.
  "Lock to First Column" keeps the audience on column 1.
- Stops and loops: ManimGX sections are click stops;
  presentation.loop repeats a part, presentation.skip goes on by
  itself. Space/PageDown forward, Shift+Space/PageUp back, also from
  the presentation window; buttons and a pause button in the
  presentation controls. Stepping centers whole pages.
- Cues: objects with `rnote_cue` set are for the lecturer only (what to
  write by hand, hints). Never in the presentation window; with a notes
  column only on the copy, otherwise on the slide.
- Pictures (ManimGX's ImageMobject) show and animate like shapes; they
  are stored as ManimGX records them (raw RGBA in the take) plus a PNG
  per still frame, so scene files should downscale photos.
- The audience always sees slides animate. The lecturer's screen shows
  the end state unless Settings > General "Animate Slides on This
  Screen".
- Update re-runs the stored scene files and replaces slides by scene
  name in place, ink kept, one undo step. Only slides whose hash
  changed run again (class, the module-level definitions it uses,
  module settings, SLIDES, local imports, ManimGX and driver version);
  Re-render All ignores the hashes.

Approach:
- crates/rnote-engine/src/manimslide/take/: reader for ManimGX's take
  format v1 and converter to keyframed paths (LINEAR when blendable,
  STEP otherwise; paint mixed in OKLab as ManimGX does). Tests compare
  renders against ManimGX's own player (tests/data/manimslide/take).
- Cue flag: the driver patches ManimGX's Feeder.record (pinned version)
  to set flag bit 1<<32 on cue records; the take format is unchanged.
- Storage: VectorImage.manim_slide (optional) holds the take (base64),
  scene name, a copy of the scene code, file, time, role (live, live
  beside notes, notes copy) and hash. svg_data is the end frame, so
  readers without slide support still show it. Old slide-JSON
  documents open as still frames.
- A picture is a textured quad: its first triangle and texture
  coordinates give the affine map from pixels to the scene. Edge pixels
  are extended and the quad clipped, as ManimGX's GPU samples them.
  Converted pictures are cached per thread for playback.
- Playback state lives in SlidePlayer beside the store, not in the
  strokes. The store draw loops of all views ask it through the
  LiveStrokes trait and draw live slides at their stacking place.
- Import converts each take once, on all cores; still frames are drawn
  sequentially (parallel cairo drawing measured many times slower).
  Update prepares replacements off the main thread.

Constraints: builds on dual-screen and projector-tablet (presentation
window, raster cache). Developed further on branch exp-manim-slides.
File format: additive optional field only. Needs uv only to import or
update, not to open or present.

